{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-28", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curves for contrast filters 00-5 (Developer MULTIGRADE 1+9, 2 min, 20 C, glossy baryta) and spectral sensitivity digitised from the Ilford MULTIGRADE FB CLASSIC technical information sheet (Oct 2013). Original data are property of Harman technology / Ilford. Family axis (development_time field) holds the contrast grade: 00=0, 0=0.5, 1..5. Exposure axis shifted per grade so that log E = 0 gives the mid-grey reflection density 0.745. All curves read from vector paths of the data sheet charts; spectral y-scale assumed 22 pt per log unit (axis unlabelled).", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; only the profile format and wavelength grid taken from spektrafilm."}, "info": {"stock": "ilford_multigrade_fb_classic", "name": "Ilford Multigrade FB Classic (Barytpapier, gl\u00e4nzend), Kontrastgrade 00\u20135", "type": "negative", "support": "paper", "stage": "printing", "use": "still", "antihalation": "weak", "target_print": null, "channel_model": "bw", "densitometer": "diffuse_visual", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 1.0, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "card": {"maker": "Ilford", "iso": null, "type": "Schwarzwei\u00dfpapier auf Baryttr\u00e4ger (FB)", "rms": null, "additional": "Kontrastgrade 00 bis 5", "text": "Das klassische Barytpapier: etwas tiefere Schwarzt\u00f6ne und feinere Tonwerte in den Lichtern als RC. Der Papiertr\u00e4ger l\u00e4sst T\u00f6ne ruhiger und dichter wirken; traditionell das Papier f\u00fcr Ausstellungsabz\u00fcge.", "source": "Ilford Multigrade FB Classic", "process": "Schwarzwei\u00df-Papierentwicklung (Barytpapier)", "suitable": ["Ausstellungsabz\u00fcge", "Landschaft und Portr\u00e4t mit tiefem Schwarz", "Tonung"], "less_suitable": ["schnelle Kontaktbogen", "Abz\u00fcge ohne lange W\u00e4sserung"], "tips": ["Papiergrad 00 bis 5 w\u00e4hlen: niedrigere Stufen sind weicher, h\u00f6here h\u00e4rter; Papier matt hebt das Schwarz leicht an.", "Der Papierton l\u00e4sst sich \u00fcber den Regler Papierton w\u00e4rmer oder k\u00fchler stellen."], "facts": [{"text": "Das Papier hat nach Datenblatt einen wei\u00dfen Tr\u00e4ger mit neutralem Bildton, 255 g/m\u00b2 und ist in Hochglanz (1K) und matt (5K) erh\u00e4ltlich; sieben volle Kontrastgrade in halben Stufen.", "source": "Ilford Multigrade FB Classic, Technical Information (2013)"}, {"text": "Es ist Teil des Multigrade-Systems und l\u00e4sst sich auch mit Negativen des Films XP2 Super verwenden; die Hochglanzvariante tont gut.", "source": "Ilford Multigrade FB Classic, Technical Information (2013)"}]}}, "data": {"wavelengths": [380.0, 385.0, 390.0, 395.0, 400.0, 405.0, 410.0, 415.0, 420.0, 425.0, 430.0, 435.0, 440.0, 445.0, 450.0, 455.0, 460.0, 465.0, 470.0, 475.0, 480.0, 485.0, 490.0, 495.0, 500.0, 505.0, 510.0, 515.0, 520.0, 525.0, 530.0, 535.0, 540.0, 545.0, 550.0, 555.0, 560.0, 565.0, 570.0, 575.0, 580.0, 585.0, 590.0, 595.0, 600.0, 605.0, 610.0, 615.0, 620.0, 625.0, 630.0, 635.0, 640.0, 645.0, 650.0, 655.0, 660.0, 665.0, 670.0, 675.0, 680.0, 685.0, 690.0, 695.0, 700.0, 705.0, 710.0, 715.0, 720.0, 725.0, 730.0, 735.0, 740.0, 745.0, 750.0, 755.0, 760.0, 765.0, 770.0, 775.0, 780.0], "log_sensiti